{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-dot/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:35.270862Z","id":"a86fae451f92d4fd8d655935d0c0467fb738e9afd2e503b0f768d3321c659127","body":{"detail":"Only `render_path` (crates/toolpath-dot/src/lib.rs:98-110, 143-149) reads `path.path.parent`. `render_graph` tracks root steps with only `base.ref_str` (lines 310-318) and draws cross-cluster edges only from a base commit that is a step in another path (lines 349-366). So `p merge examples/path-02-local-session.path.json examples/path-05-continuation.path.json | p render dot` puts both paths in one graph yet draws no edge from path-session-xyz/step-003 to the continuation's root step-004, and shows no PARENT node either; the parent appears nowhere in the DOT output. The Markdown renderer prints it for each path in a graph because render_graph there calls write_path_context (crates/toolpath-md/src/lib.rs:247,252), so the two renderers now disagree. CHANGELOG.md:24-25 scopes the DOT change to 'the path layout', which is accurate but leaves the gap unrecorded.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":310},"end":{"line":366},"content_hash":"74d6f7f8db51ad44b6986632efd3ba072263389566a1f719ab92921620c87f24"},"suggested_fix":"In render_graph, for each root step of a path with `parent` set: when a path with id `parent.path` holding step `parent.step` is in the graph, draw `parent.step -> root` as a cross-cluster edge like the base-commit edge; otherwise draw a per-path PARENT node (unique id such as `__parent_{i}__`) with the escaped uri/path/step label. Add a test with a two-path graph.","summary":"toolpath-dot render_graph ignores path.parent, so the graph layout draws no lineage while the Markdown graph layout prints it","tags":["review","review:pr-354-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-dot/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:14:02.179452Z","id":"cb9bf9642e658fe47a2e0d5796a680fbb2ffa3316a200d43b7498b639456846c","body":{"detail":"Only render_path reads path.parent (crates/toolpath-dot/src/lib.rs:98-110,142-149). render_graph records root steps with base ref_str only (lines 310-318) and cross-cluster edges only from commit_to_step (349-366). Ran: target/debug/path p merge examples/path-02-local-session.path.json examples/path-05-continuation.path.json > merged.json; path p render dot --input merged.json | grep -i 'parent\\|-> \"step-004\"' prints only the step-004 node line (no PARENT node, no edge into step-004). path p render md --input merged.json prints line 51: **Parent:** `file:///home/alex/.toolpath/path-02-local-session.path.json` path `path-session-xyz` @ `step-003` (via write_path_context, crates/toolpath-md/src/lib.rs:247,252). suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"a86fae451f92d4fd8d655935d0c0467fb738e9afd2e503b0f768d3321c659127","summary":"confirmed: render_graph draws no lineage for path.parent while the Markdown graph render prints it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
